  "slug": "rna-seq-large-language-0072",
  "summary": "Nanopore modification data, microbial variant prioritization, and reproducible metagenomic pipelines are now being packaged as usable tools.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational tooling for bacterial and microbial sequence data, with emphasis on prioritization and reproducible execution. Snappy applies graph-based motif enrichment to basecaller modification data from Oxford Nanopore reads to identify bacterial DNA methylation motifs. SNPraefentia, a Python toolkit, ranks microbial metagenomic SNPs by a composite score combining depth, amino acid impact, and UniProt protein-domain annotation. MeTAline packages shotgun metagenomic taxonomic and functional profiling as an open-source Snakemake pipeline with Docker and Singularity containers. The Pseudomonas genomic islands study is a biological analysis rather than a tool, reporting defence and anti-defence hotspots with 11 conserved loci recurring beyond island contexts. What is new across the set is methylation-motif identification directly from nanopore modification data and explicit composite prioritization of microbial variants.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-25"
}
